# Trivy ignore file for vulnerabilities without available fixes.
# Mostly OS-level CVEs in the ubuntu:26.04 base that don't have patches yet,
# plus a few documented false-positives. CVEs that DO have a fix are patched at
# the source (base/package upgrade or binary removal) rather than ignored here —
# see the Canonical Pebble note at the bottom of this file for an example.

# coreutils - low severity, very old CVE
CVE-2016-2781

# gpgv - low priority
CVE-2022-3219

# libgcrypt20 - waiting for Ubuntu patches
CVE-2024-2236

# openssl/libssl3t64 - waiting for Ubuntu patches
CVE-2024-41996

# login/passwd - waiting for Ubuntu patches
CVE-2024-56433

# tar - waiting for Ubuntu patches
CVE-2025-45582

# libexpat1 - waiting for Ubuntu patches
CVE-2025-66382

# go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk - FALSE POSITIVE
# CVE-2026-39883 (PATH hijacking via kenv on BSD) is fixed in v1.43.0.
# We are on v1.43.0. Trivy's database incorrectly flags it — the affected
# range is < 1.43.0. Remove this entry once Trivy's DB is corrected.
# https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-39883
CVE-2026-39883

# NOTE on Canonical Pebble (/usr/bin/pebble) in the ubuntu base:
# That stray Go binary (github.com/canonical/pebble, vendoring an old
# golang.org/x/net + older Go stdlib) used to flag a cluster of HIGH CVEs
# (CVE-2026-25680/25681/27136/27145/39821/42502/42506, and on newer base
# digests also -33814 / -42504). We do NOT ignore those — our containers never
# invoke pebble, so every ubuntu-based Dockerfile — the scanned trio
# Dockerfile.{server,ac.aws,relay}, the un-gated Dockerfile.{ac,app,base}, and
# the local/CI smoke image tests/smoke/local-stack/Dockerfile — deletes
# /usr/bin/pebble. scripts/check-base-image-pebble-purge.sh enforces that at PR
# time so a new/edited ubuntu Dockerfile can't silently skip it. Trivy
# scans the squashed filesystem, so removing the binary drops the whole gobinary
# target to zero findings — fixable CVEs are fixed, not suppressed. If a future
# base ever legitimately needs pebble, revisit (bump to a digest whose pebble
# vendors x/net >= 0.55.0 and Go >= 1.26.4) rather than adding ignores here.
